invariant: INV-14
file: widemul.h
catches: tcp_blocking_loop_widemul
reason: widemul_answer_ok admits ch_cfg.widemul at 0, the value a caller that
  never set the field leaves, and the session runs as though the caller
  had answered CH_WIDEMUL_NOT_STATED. The ruling is that every caller
  states its answer (docs/decisions.md 87). The edit keeps 3 refused, so
  it moves the lower edge alone; test/tcp_blocking_loop_widemul.h
  requires ch_connect to refuse 0 before a byte leaves.

--- old
    return cfg->widemul == CH_WIDEMUL_CONSTANT_TIME || cfg->widemul == CH_WIDEMUL_NOT_STATED;
--- new
    return cfg->widemul <= CH_WIDEMUL_NOT_STATED;
